---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const EMAIL = "hello@tmke.co.uk";
const UPDATED = "16 June 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cookie Policy — TMKE"
  description="The cookies and similar storage TMKE uses, and how to control them."
  noindex
>
  <main class="legal">
    <div class="legal-inner">
      <p class="legal-eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="legal-title">Cookie Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: {UPDATED}</p>

      <p>
        This policy explains the cookies and similar technologies (such as browser <em>localStorage</em>)
        we use on this website, and how you can control them. It sits alongside our
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>1. What these technologies are</h2>
      <p>
        Cookies and local storage are small pieces of data saved in your browser. Some are essential to make
        a website work; others help measure how a site is used. Under UK rules (PECR), anything that isn’t
        strictly necessary may only be used with your consent.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Your choice</h2>
      <p>
        When you first visit, we ask whether to enable non-essential (analytics) storage. We don’t set any
        analytics storage unless you select <strong>“Accept all”</strong>. You can change your mind at any
        time — <a href="#" data-cookie-settings>open cookie settings</a> — or clear cookies/storage in your
        browser settings. Essential items below are always on, because the site can’t function without them.
      </p>

      <h2>3. What we use</h2>

      <h3>Strictly necessary (always on)</h3>
      <table class="legal-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Name / type</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Set by</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>tmke-consent</code> (localStorage)</td><td>Remembers your cookie choice so we don’t ask again.</td><td>TMKE</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Authentication session (localStorage)</td><td>Keeps you signed in to your account.</td><td>Our authentication provider</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Security cookies (e.g. <code>__cf_bm</code>, <code>cf_clearance</code>)</td><td>Protect the site against bots and abuse, and keep it reliable.</td><td>Our hosting/security provider</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Anti-bot challenge</td><td>Checks form submissions are from a person, not a bot.</td><td>Our hosting/security provider</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h3>Analytics (only with your consent)</h3>
      <table class="legal-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Name / type</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Set by</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>tmke-sid</code> (localStorage)</td><td>A random identifier so we can count visits and understand journeys through the site, without identifying you personally.</td><td>TMKE</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>tmke-pv-fired</code> (sessionStorage)</td><td>Notes that a visit has been recorded this session, so we don’t double-count.</td><td>TMKE</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="legal-note">
        These are only created after you select “Accept all”. If you reject non-essential storage, no analytics
        identifiers are stored and no usage events are recorded.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Managing cookies in your browser</h2>
      <p>
        You can block or delete cookies and clear local storage through your browser settings. Doing so may
        affect parts of the site that rely on essential storage (for example staying signed in).
      </p>

      <h2>5. Questions</h2>
      <p>Email us at <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a> with any questions about this policy.</p>

      <p class="legal-foot"><a href="/">&larr; Back to TMKE</a></p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
